  "content": {
    "id": "p32-q70-group-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Complete the square of the following by adding the $2ab$ term.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p32-q70-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$x^2+1$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+1)^2-2x$ or $(x-1)^2+2x$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+1&=x^2+2x+1-2x\\\\x^2+1&=(x+1)^2-2x.\\end{align*}$$\nAlternatively, use the negative middle term:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+1&=x^2-2x+1+2x\\\\x^2+1&=(x-1)^2+2x.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q71-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$4a^2+9$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2a+3)^2-12a$ or $(2a-3)^2+12a$.",
          "worked": "The middle term is $2(2a)(3)=12a$.\n$$\\begin{align*}4a^2+9&=4a^2+12a+9-12a\\\\4a^2+9&=(2a+3)^2-12a.\\end{align*}$$\nAlternatively:\n$$\\begin{align*}4a^2+9&=4a^2-12a+9+12a\\\\4a^2+9&=(2a-3)^2+12a.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q72-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$x^2+\\frac1{x^2}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(x+\\dfrac1x\\right)^2-2$ or $\\left(x-\\dfrac1x\\right)^2+2$, where $x\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, the middle term is $2x\\left(\\frac1x\\right)=2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+\\frac1{x^2}&=x^2+2+\\frac1{x^2}-2\\\\x^2+\\frac1{x^2}&=\\left(x+\\frac1x\\right)^2-2.\\end{align*}$$\nAlternatively:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2+\\frac1{x^2}&=x^2-2+\\frac1{x^2}+2\\\\x^2+\\frac1{x^2}&=\\left(x-\\frac1x\\right)^2+2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p32-q73-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$25+\\frac1{4t^2}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(5+\\dfrac1{2t}\\right)^2-\\dfrac5t$ or $\\left(5-\\dfrac1{2t}\\right)^2+\\dfrac5t$, where $t\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "For $t\\ne0$, the middle term is $2(5)\\left(\\frac1{2t}\\right)=\\frac5t$.\n$$\\begin{align*}25+\\frac1{4t^2}&=25+\\frac5t+\\frac1{4t^2}-\\frac5t\\\\25+\\frac1{4t^2}&=\\left(5+\\frac1{2t}\\right)^2-\\frac5t.\\end{align*}$$\nAlternatively:\n$$\\begin{align*}25+\\frac1{4t^2}&=25-\\frac5t+\\frac1{4t^2}+\\frac5t\\\\25+\\frac1{4t^2}&=\\left(5-\\frac1{2t}\\right)^2+\\frac5t.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
  },
